From af7d4fbbfd8374e4c27c706e1c96218280f3b201 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woksin <sindrewilting@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:44:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Add replica-set fault matrix and unit specs for the
 MongoDB writer fence

Covers revocation at every pause point of a batch, a late command from a
revoked owner, a writer that died mid-batch, unknown commit outcomes
(committed, not committed, revoked, left open), racing claims, fenced DDL,
and the fenced sink writes. The history oracle has a planted-write
self-check, and CHRONICLE_FENCE_SPECS_UNFENCED=1 bypasses the fence for
stale writers to prove the revocation specs fail without it.
